<title>HONDURAS: Exporter says Honduran cattle smuggled to Mexico.</title>
<headline>Exporter says Honduran cattle smuggled to Mexico.</headline>
<dateline>TEGUCIGALPA, Honduras 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Some 250,000 heads of Honduran cattle have been smuggled to Mexico in 1996, the director of Honduras' Meat Exporters Association, Armando Erazo, said Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;I calculate that at least 250,000 heads of cattle have been smuggled to Mexico,&quot; Erazo told reporters.</p>
<p>Lower meat prices in the United States and Mexican tariffs of 25 percent on Central American meat products have led to the smuggling, he said.</p>
<p>--Tegucigalpa bureau, (504) 392-885</p>
